(18647970, 'Sarah Thankam Mathews', 'Thankam: thun like thunder, gum like gumdrop. Mathews with one T: the Keralite way. Any pronouns. Grew up between Oman and India, immigrating to the US in my late teens. Organizes sometimes: climate, immigration, mutual aid. Debut novel All This Could Be Different, shortlisted for the 2022 National Book Award, Discover Prize, Aspen Literary Prize. Work in Best American Short Stories 2020 and other places. Proud product of public schools. Lives in Brooklyn, New York. Grateful for anyone who has read my book!', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1678202915p5/18647970.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/photo.php?fbid=884998210297458&id=100063618611771&set=a.124193359711284', 'https://www.instagram.com/smathewss/?hl=en', '', 'https://www.smathewss.com/', 1),
(18692517, 'Kate Elizabeth Russell', 'Kate Elizabeth Russell was born and raised in eastern Maine. She holds an MFA from Indiana University and a PhD from the University of Kansas. My Dark Vanessa is her debut novel.', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1672760445p5/18692517.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/photo.php?fbid=10158187304754712&id=235401934711&set=a.10153085512284712', 'https://www.instagram.com/kateelizabethrussell/?hl=en', '', 'https://kateelizabethrussell.com/', 1),
(18765341, 'Melody Raven', 'Melody Raven is a Michigan girl through and through. She is overly attached to her rescue pit bull, Rigby, and spends her time not writing chasing all sorts of worldly pleasures.She travels all over the world, devours entertainment in any form, from books to movies to podcasts, and collects amazing experiences like a hoarder on a TV show. Melody also writes romantic suspense and contemporary romance under the name Mallory Crowe. Her life\'s motto is \"if it\'s worth doing, it\'s worth overdoing\".', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1607886857p5/18765341.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/Melody-Raven-440977839770374/', 'https://www.instagram.com/melody.raven/', 'https://www.youtube.com/@RavenMelodyChannel/streams', 'http://www.melodyravenbooks.com/', 1),
(18858017, 'Lily  Archer', 'When I began writing Taylor and Leander\'s story, I had NO idea it would capture so many of your hearts and imaginations. Thank you for loving them as much as I do. You are making my dreams come true.Lily Archer believes in fairies, mermaids, and fierce fae warriors. Armed with nothing more than her imagination and a well-worn MacBook, she intends to slay the darkest beasts of the fantasy worlds and create true love where none seemed possible.Visit me at www.lilyarcherauthor.com', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1549539525p5/18858017.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/LilyArcherAuthor/', 'https://www.instagram.com/lilyarcher_/', 'https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCmdlsgX1MUT82xXIN82g6yA', 'https://www.lilyarcherauthor.com/', 1),
(18877437, 'Tilly Hart', '', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1591358533p5/18877437.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/tillyhartauthor/', 'https://www.instagram.com/tilly.hart/?hl=en', 'https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCsKsAHboT-1HHszUTZSEPCQ/videos', 'https://www.instagram.com/tilly.hart/?hl=en', 1),
(18898964, 'Diana Logan', '', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1550838017p5/18898964.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/public/Diana-Logan/', 'https://www.instagram.com/dianalogan184/', 'https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCdKnwOIlFYZe83moWQ-aDwA?feature=applinks', 'http://dianalogan.com/', 1),
(18910992, 'Catherine Adel West', 'Catherine Adel West was born and raised in Chicago, where she currently resides. She graduated with both her Bachelors and Masters of Science in Journalism from the University of Illinois - Urbana. Her work is published in Black Fox Literary Magazine, Five2One, Better than Starbucks, Doors Ajar, 805 Lit + Art, The Helix Magazine, Lunch Ticket and Gay Magazine. Author of Saving Ruby King, Catherine was named one of USA TODAYS Black Authors You Should Know. The Two Lives of Sara is her sophomore novel.', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1589639198p5/18910992.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/cathy.west.5015/', 'https://www.instagram.com/cawest329/p/C_v8moNSqOD/', 'https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCRQWLIJbJuhI239gBivmKbQ/featured', 'https://www.catherineadelwest.com/', 1),
(18919679, 'Ava York', 'Reader, dreamer and frantic scribbler. I really do believe that love conquers all... and make terrible things for my characters to survive to prove it! (insert evil laugh here)', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1603305197p5/18919679.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/avayorkauthor/', 'https://www.instagram.com/_avayork_/?hl=en', 'https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCmgh0en304kLmf6NYjxUYZQ', 'https://avayorkbooks.com/', 1),
(18923983, 'Lux Miller', '', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1564160609p5/18923983.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/story.php?story_fbid=1166496211156033&id=100033869955935', 'https://www.instagram.com/luxmiller28/', 'https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC5pmtm4Dg4f8jlVjmxcJ0uw', 'https://luxmillerauthor.wixsite.com/home', 1),
(18997169, 'A.D. Key', 'The Blooded series is now under Chelsea Vale:https://www.goodreads.com/author/show...', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1600385487p5/18997169.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/AdkeyOfficial/', 'https://www.instagram.com/adkey.agency/', 'https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCBMUQwqK_RLybqh52NiNM5w', 'https://www.advanced-diagnostics.com/', 1),
(19024662, 'Avery Song', '', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1556794599p5/19024662.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/averysongauthor/', 'https://www.instagram.com/averysongauthor/p/DCSJQBBJz1z/', 'https://www.youtube.com/@averyofficial', 'https://www.facebook.com/averysongauthor/', 1),
(19053518, 'Eliza Raine', 'Eliza Raine writes Greek mythology inspired fantasy that is fast paced, full of new worlds and creatures and sprinkled with a healthy dose of romance. She lives near Reading in England with her husband, three cats and outrageously cute puppy. She has a BA Hons in History and has a deep-rooted passion for mythology and stories about women who don\'t need rescuing.She can usually be found reading fairytale retellings, playing board games or binge-watching Netflix shows.You can read some of Eliza\'s stories for free by visiting her website at www.elizaraine.com', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1559568133p5/19053518.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/elizaraineauthor/', 'https://www.instagram.com/elizaraineauthor/', 'https://www.youtube.com/c/DisabledEliza/about', 'https://www.elizaraine.com/', 1),
(19080346, 'Bailey Dark', 'Bailey Dark is obsessed with all things dark, hot, and supernatural.From Fae to Aliens, her heroes are thoroughly alpha and pure raw masculinity. When she\'s not writing (which is hardly ever) she\'s busy watching every movie in the marvel universe, or binging supernatural on her couch.So come along, and enter her dark world. . . .Website: https://www.baileydarkromance.com/CONTACT: BAILEYDARKROMANCE@GMAIL.COM', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1594750324p5/19080346.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/baileysarian1/', 'https://www.instagram.com/baileyblackphoto/?hl=en', 'https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLCprSpAj-wvAeHWGzQ-JgTyljg6GyC9D1', 'https://baileysarian.com/?srsltid=AfmBOoqFFoCfYyRb87xdvnA8pugt3s1PMrRlEz_BsNgL5oRlzE8ZRaLT', 1),
(19103305, 'Carina Taylor', 'No Description available', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1639096024p5/19103305.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/carinataylorauthor/', 'https://www.instagram.com/carinataylorauthor/?hl=en', 'https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCP2vhOonxtIEcJ6UAyFSZpw', 'https://carinataylorbooks.com/', 1),
(19122506, 'Luke Johnston', 'No Description available', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/No-Image-Placeholder.svg/1665px-No-Image-Placeholder.svg.png', 'https://www.facebook.com/public/Luke-Johnston/', 'https://www.instagram.com/luke_johnston/', 'https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC_tcMWFzGBJ_PEItu7EqmUg', 'https://goprincetontigers.com/sports/mens-water-polo/roster/luke-johnston/21446', 1),
(19186732, 'Erin Cain', '', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/No-Image-Placeholder.svg/1665px-No-Image-Placeholder.svg.png', 'https://www.facebook.com/public/Erin-Cain/', 'https://www.instagram.com/erincain/', 'https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCOdN--4v7kfA6ZVz62NN34w', 'http://www.erincain.com/', 1),
(19190935, 'R. Eric Thomas', 'R. Eric Thomas (he/him) is a national bestselling author, playwright, and screenwriter. His books include, Here for It, or How to Save Your Soul in America, which was featured as a Read with Jenna pick on NBC\'s Today, Reclaiming Her Time: The Power of Maxine Waters, co-authored with Helena Andrews-Dyer, the YA novel Kings of B’more, a 2023 American Library Association Stonewall Honor book, and the essay collection Congratulations, the Best Is Over! For his playwriting, Eric has won the Barrymore Award for Best New Play, the Dramatist Guild Lanford Wilson Award, the Lambda Literary Award, and was a finalist for the Steinberg/ATCA New Play Award. On screen, he wrote for the Peabody Award-winning series Dickinson on AppleTV+ and Better Things', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1590615425p5/19190935.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/R.Eric.T/', 'https://www.instagram.com/oureric/?hl=en', 'https://www.youtube.com/user/etthehiphoppreacher', 'https://rericthomas.com/', 1),
(19227365, 'Atlas Rose', 'Dark Romance Author who loves forbidden romance.➣ Blood Ties Series➣ The Institute Series➣ Mafia Monster Series', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1661791372p5/19227365.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/AtlasRoseRomance/', 'https://www.instagram.com/atlasroseromance/?hl=en', 'https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCTUqfO1BviNG6ZcXuIJswlg', 'https://atlasrosedarkromance.com/?srsltid=AfmBOopeVjHjkjElIFIKAohTmnARDIvFLASqJGg_j1N6dAWWcTsr4LZa', 1),
(19250455, 'Megha Majumdar', 'MEGHA MAJUMDAR was born and raised in Kolkata, India. She moved to the United States to attend college at Harvard University, followed by graduate school in social anthropology at Johns Hopkins University. She works as an editor at Catapult, and lives in New York City. A Burning is her first book. Follow her on Twitter @MeghaMaj and Instagram @megha.maj', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1575903756p5/19250455.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/megha.majumdar.1/', 'https://www.instagram.com/megha.maj/?hl=en', 'https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCTfAdJcJFeSSZTDpm07k22g', 'https://www.meghamajumdar.com/', 1),
(19278992, 'Jesse Q. Sutanto', 'Jesse Q Sutanto grew up shuttling back and forth between Jakarta and Singapore and sees both cities as her homes. She has a Masters degree from Oxford University, though she has yet to figure out a way of saying that without sounding obnoxious. She is currently living back in Jakarta on the same street as her parents and about seven hundred meddlesome aunties. When she\'s not tearing out her hair over her latest WIP, she spends her time baking and playing FPS games. Oh, and also being a mom to her two kids.', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1564130716p5/19278992.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/JesseQSutanto/', 'https://www.instagram.com/jesseqsutanto/?hl=en', '', 'https://jesseqsutantoauthor.com/', 1),
(19283434, 'Onley James', 'Onley James lives in North Carolina with her daughter, her daughter-in-law, son-in-law, and a menagerie of animals, both good and evil. James splits her time between writing m/m romance and mainlining dangerous levels of caffeine and attempting to maintain her ever-slipping sanity.When not at her desk you can find her whining about how much writing she has to do while avoiding said writing by binge-watching unhealthy amounts of television and doom scrolling on social media. She loves true crime documentaries, anti-heroes, and writing kinky, snarky books about morally gray men who fall in love with other men.Stay up to date: www.onleyjames.com/newsletterFind me on Facebook: https://www.facebook.com/groups/Onley...Want more: linktr.ee/OnleyJa', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1562751774p5/19283434.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/onleyjameswrites/', 'https://www.instagram.com/onleyjameswrites/?hl=en', 'https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCV5Gw7GGOMxe6SSF6llp_3Q', 'https://www.onleyjames.com/', 1),
(19318051, 'Afia Atakora', '', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1564137262p5/19318051.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/AfiaAtakoraAuthor/', 'https://www.instagram.com/afiaatakora/', 'https://www.youtube.com/c/ReadingCoveBookClub/videos', 'https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/authors/2175078/afia-atakora/', 1),
(19347143, 'Asha Lemmie', 'Asha Lemmie is the New York Times bestselling author of Fifty Words For Rain and The Wildest Sun. She holds a BA in English Literature from Boston College and is currently a graduate student at Columbia University. She resides in New York City but can frequently be found wandering. Asha writes historical fiction that focuses on bringing unique perspectives to life.', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1679695036p5/19347143.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/events/d41d8cd9/alka-joshi-author-of-the-secret-keeper-of-jaipur-in-conversation-with-asha-lemmi/1192869121154266/', 'https://www.instagram.com/ashalemmieauthor/?hl=en', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9h6SRnHRtIs', 'https://www.bc.edu/bc-web/schools/morrissey/departments/english/about/news-and-notes/debut-novel-by-asha-lemmie.html', 1),
(19363906, 'Ash Davidson', 'Ash Davidson spent her early years in Klamath, California, and attended the Iowa Writers’ Workshop. Her work has been supported by the Arizona Commission on the Arts, MacDowell, Monson Arts, and the National Endowment for the Arts. She lives in Flagstaff, Arizona.', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1604392890p5/19363906.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/ash.davidson.writer/', 'https://www.instagram.com/ashdavidsonwriter/?hl=en', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MzQZioQuzpY', 'https://www.ashdavidson.net/', 1),
(19419814, 'Lexxi James', 'Lexxi James | Author of Hot Romance & Happily Ever Afters ❤️As a USA Today Bestselling author, Lexxi James has hit the top 50 bestseller lists on Amazon, Apple Books, and Barnes & Noble, with books sold in over 26 countries. Best known for seductive romantic suspense, she loves matching smoking hot heroes with their soul mates. Her signature style is witty banter, high heat, and a whole lot of heart. She proudly calls the Midwest home where she lives with the man of her dreams and the sweetest daughter in the universe. Her pastimes include reading, loading up on unhealthy quantities of caffeine, and binging Netflix and reality TV. She’s a sucker for kids selling cookies and pretty much anything on Etsy. To receive hot romances with happily', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1642858325p5/19419814.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/LexxiJames/', 'https://www.instagram.com/lexxijamesbooks/?hl=en', 'https://www.youtube.com/channel/UClOJ5iQJhf2WD5AxY-kZnHw', 'https://www.lexxijames.com/', 1),
(19420282, 'Bryan Arneson', 'No Author Description', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/No-Image-Placeholder.svg/1665px-No-Image-Placeholder.svg.png', 'https://www.facebook.com/bryan.arneson/', 'https://www.instagram.com/bryan_ameson/?hl=en', 'https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC__ackViVUkqJwBprspjJ0A', '/search?num=12', 1),
(19429945, 'Bryan Morrison', 'No Description available', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/No-Image-Placeholder.svg/1665px-No-Image-Placeholder.svg.png', 'https://www.facebook.com/public/Bryan-Morrison/', 'https://www.instagram.com/bryangmorrison/', 'https://www.youtube.com/@bryanmorrison8833', 'https://www.instagram.com/bryangmorrison/', 1),
(19532769, 'Anna Heskin', '', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1568479533p5/19532769.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/annaheskin/', 'https://www.instagram.com/annaheskin/', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rCy0tNLOJ54', 'https://www.amazon.com/stores/author/B07XKBFTXS', 1),
(19553489, 'Ronnie Whitlock', 'No Author Description', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/No-Image-Placeholder.svg/1665px-No-Image-Placeholder.svg.png', 'https://www.facebook.com/ronnie.whitlock.3/', 'https://www.instagram.com/pharaohzhoundz/', 'https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCqubJzhRAbS3LYm4aHZUtTQ', 'https://www.linkedin.com/in/ronnie-whitlock-83aa7b74', 1),
(19585207, 'Vivian Lark', '', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/No-Image-Placeholder.svg/1665px-No-Image-Placeholder.svg.png', 'https://www.facebook.com/vivian.lark.77/', 'https://www.instagram.com/vivianlarkstudios/', 'https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC5SOfnUmhC4-nJIZA8tPs9Q', 'https://www.vivianlark.com/', 1),
(19595183, 'Juhea Kim', 'Juhea Kim\'s bestselling debut novel, Beasts of a Little Land, was named a finalist for the 2022 Dayton Literary Peace Prize and shortlisted for the 2024 Yasnaya Polyana Award, Russia\'s biggest annual literary prize awarded by the Tolstoy Estate-Museum. It has been published in 13 countries to date and a TV series adaptation is currently in development. She donates a portion of the proceeds of Beasts of a Little Land to Siberian tiger and Amur leopard conservation.Juhea\'s second novel, City of Night Birds, is forthcoming in November 2024. She donates a portion of the proceeds of City of Night Birds to Caritas Somalia, a development and emergency aid NGO. Her writing has been published in Granta, Slice, Zyzzyva, Catapult, Guernica, Shenandoah', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1616573993p5/19595183.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/photo.php?fbid=10159207045165020&id=9122810019&set=a.121195860019', 'https://www.instagram.com/juhea_writes/?hl=en', 'https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCUjzlKgL_LPYGuV8W3MX8gA/videos', 'https://www.juheakim.com/', 1),
(19595208, 'Maria Dean', '', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/No-Image-Placeholder.svg/1665px-No-Image-Placeholder.svg.png', 'https://www.facebook.com/p/Author-Maria-Dean-100036881096839/', 'https://www.instagram.com/mariaadean/?hl=en', 'https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCRAOOhvDibzu7ODuIVIojlA/videos', 'https://authormariadean.com/', 1),
(19607931, 'Megan Nolan', 'Megan Nolan was born in 1990 in Waterford, Ireland and is currently based in London. Her essays and reviews have been published by the New York Times, White Review, Guardian and Frieze amongst others. Her debut novel, Acts of Desperation, was published by Jonathan Cape in 2021 and was the recipient of a Betty Trask Award, shortlisted for the Sunday Times Young Writer of the Year Award and longlisted for the Dylan Thomas Prize.Her second novel, Ordinary Human Failings, will be published by Jonathan Cape in July 2023.', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1680281586p5/19607931.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/public/Megan-Nolan/', 'https://www.instagram.com/mmegannolan/?hl=en', 'https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC57xg7pEwPF5Zx_OpY0lI9Q', 'http://megannolan.org/', 1),
(19778145, 'Destiny Roberts', '', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/No-Image-Placeholder.svg/1665px-No-Image-Placeholder.svg.png', 'https://www.facebook.com/destiny.roberts/', 'https://www.instagram.com/dezzyraww/?hl=en', 'https://www.youtube.com/c/DestinyRoberts', 'https://www.instagram.com/dezzyraww/?hl=en', 1),
(19788573, 'Sarah Penner', 'NYT Bestselling author of The Lost Apothecary (Park Row Books/HarperCollins), to be translated into 40 languages worldwide. To learn more, visit SarahPenner.com.', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1582667763p5/19788573.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/sarah.blacker.39/', 'https://www.instagram.com/sarah_penner_author/?hl=en', 'https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCsKcEnxV6GS0C0XQL-te9xA', 'https://www.sarahpenner.com/', 1),
(19812297, 'Jean Chen Ho', 'Jean Chen Ho is a writer in Los Angeles. She was born in Taiwan and grew up in Southern California. Jean is the author of Fiona and Jane (Viking, 2022), a linked story collection. She\'s a doctoral candidate in Creative Writing and Literature at the University of Southern California, where she is a Dornsife Fellow in fiction. Her writing is published in Georgia Review, GQ, Harper’s Bazaar, Guernica, The Rumpus, Apogee, McSweeney\'s Internet Tendency, and others. She holds an MFA in Creative Writing from the University of Nevada, Las Vegas.', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1618066568p5/19812297.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/events/university-of-st-thomas/diverse-voices-author-series-jean-chen-ho/1181073629094353/', 'https://www.instagram.com/jeanho66/?hl=en', 'https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCuom-8vq13t-1slisu1hQWA', 'https://www.jean-chen-ho.com/', 1),
(19847939, 'Stella Rue', '', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/No-Image-Placeholder.svg/1665px-No-Image-Placeholder.svg.png', 'https://www.facebook.com/stella.rue/', 'https://www.instagram.com/thelifeofstellarue/?hl=en', 'https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCsMly7xjNG5sVzBbOdgQ-9A', 'https://www.stellaandrue.com/', 1);
INSERT INTO `authors` (`id`, `name`, `info`, `image`, `facebook_url`, `instagram_url`, `youtube_url`, `website_url`, `status`) VALUES
(19926652, 'Ashley Winstead', 'Ashley Winstead is a chameleon writing across as many genres as she can get away with. Her bestselling, critically-acclaimed books have been translated into more than a dozen languages, optioned for television, named Library Read, Loan Star, and Amazon Editor picks, and covered everywhere from the New York Times to People magazine. She\'s a former academic who lives in Houston with her husband, three cats, and beloved wine fridge.', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1636826749p5/19926652.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/ashley.winstead.9/', 'https://www.instagram.com/ashleywinsteadbooks/?hl=en', 'https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCOez1VyVNebgsgOoerLh5Bg/about', 'https://www.ashleywinstead.com/', 1),
(19926921, 'Mark Bergen', '', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/No-Image-Placeholder.svg/1665px-No-Image-Placeholder.svg.png', 'https://www.facebook.com/public/Mark-Bergen/city/Charleston-South-Carolina-105557439477766/', 'https://www.instagram.com/mark_bergen/?hl=en', 'https://www.youtube.com/@MarcBergen', 'https://www.markhbergen.com/', 1),
(19981845, 'Newt Scamander', 'Pen name used by J.K. Rowling', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/No-Image-Placeholder.svg/1665px-No-Image-Placeholder.svg.png', 'https://www.facebook.com/photo.php?fbid=386534080328385&set=a.386534060328387&type=3', 'https://www.instagram.com/scamanderbrothers/?hl=en', 'https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/newtscamander', 'https://www.jkrowling.com/book/fantastic-beasts-find/', 1),
(20004876, 'Emilia  Rose', 'With over thirty-one million online story views, Emilia Rose is a USA Today bestselling author of steamy romance. She loves writing about dirty-talking bad boys and alpha-holes. She currently lives in a small town in Connecticut USA with her husband, two cats, and cute little yellow ducklings.', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1658587357p5/20004876.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/authoremiliarose/', 'https://www.instagram.com/emiliarxse/?hl=en', 'https://www.youtube.com/c/emiliarose', 'https://www.emiliarose.com/', 1),
(20050406, 'Zakiya Dalila Harris', 'Zakiya Dalila Harris spent nearly three years in editorial at Knopf/Doubleday before leaving to write her debut novel The Other Black Girl. Prior to working in publishing, Zakiya received her MFA in creative writing from The New School. Her essays and book reviews have appeared in Cosmopolitan, Guernica, and The Rumpus. She lives in Brooklyn.', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1649855065p5/20050406.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/story.php/?story_fbid=785191607132270&id=100069243132579', 'https://www.instagram.com/zakiyadalilaharris/?hl=en', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5hAZddbiWTE', 'http://zakiyadalilaharris.com/', 1),
(20144780, 'Robert Jones Jr.', 'Formerly known as “Son of Baldwin,” Robert Jones, Jr. is a Brooklyn-based, award-winning writer. He is the author of The New York Times bestselling novel, The Prophets, which won the 2022 Publishing Triangle Edmund White Award for Debut Fiction, and was a finalist for the 2021 National Book Award for Fiction. His work has been featured in The New York Times, Essence, Variety, and The Paris Review, as well as in the critically acclaimed anthologies Four Hundred Souls and The 1619 Project. He is currently working on his next novel.To keep up-to-date with his latest writings, news, musings, and events, subscribe to his newsletter, Witness: https://robertjonesjr.substack.com/p/... and visit his website: https://sonofbaldwin.com.', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1675270052p5/20144780.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/robert.j.junior.3/', 'https://www.instagram.com/robertjones_jr/?hl=en', 'https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCfA8piHwAu6D4nfZmI1IqRw', 'https://www.sonofbaldwin.com/', 1),
(20193538, 'Emma Brodie', '', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1617672049p5/20193538.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/emma.trotman/', 'https://www.instagram.com/typically_emma/', 'https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCkxtldJ1RBgF-cqMm5-a6oQ', 'https://emmabrodie.com/', 1),
(20196638, 'Mateo Askaripour', '“A month ago, I’d never heard of Mateo Askaripour. Today I would buy anything from him.”—Ron Charles,  The Washington PostMateo Askaripour wants people to feel seen. His first novel, Black Buck, takes on racism in corporate America with humor and wit. It was an instant New York Times bestseller and a Read with Jenna Today show book club pick. Askaripour was chosen as one of Entertainment Weekly’s “10 rising stars poised to make waves” and was named as a recipient of the National Book Foundation’s “5 Under 35” prize. This Great Hemisphere, published in July 2024, is his second novel. He lives in Brooklyn. Follow him on Instagram @AskMateo.', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1719507684p5/20196638.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/photo.php?fbid=1035493391913297&id=100063579370848&set=a.898083995654238&locale=zh_HK', 'https://www.instagram.com/askmateo/?hl=en', '', 'https://www.mateowrites.com/', 1),
(20270756, 'Kirthana Ramisetti', 'Kirthana Ramisetti worked in media for over ten years before trying her hand at fiction. She received her MFA in creative writing from Emerson College, and her work has appeared in Newsday, The Wall Street Journal, The Atlantic and more. A pop culture addict whose brain is a repository for random information, she’d make an excellent addition to your trivia team. Her debut novel, Dava Shastri’s Last Day, will be published in December 2021.', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1618443701p5/20270756.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/photo.php?fbid=10160045774304216&id=123349774215&set=a.10156856229634216', 'https://www.instagram.com/kirthanaramisetti/?hl=en', 'https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCIZV2cVJw0Jzf-8RuhHrKnw/videos', 'https://kirthanaramisetti.com/', 1),
(20650250, 'Nita Prose', 'NITA PROSE is the #1 New York Times bestselling author of The Mystery Guest and The Maid, which has sold more than two million copies worldwide. A Good Morning America Book Club pick, The Maid won the Ned Kelly Award for International Crime Fiction, the Fingerprint Award for Debut Book of the Year, the Anthony Award for Best First Novel, and the Barry Award for Best First Mystery. The Maid was also an Edgar Award finalist for Best Novel. Visit Nita at nitaprose.com or on Instagram and X @NitaProse.', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1619360173p5/20650250.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/KristinHarmelAuthor/posts/nita-prose-the-maid-is-back-with-the-mystery-guest-another-winning-page-turner-f/898609918555170/', 'https://www.instagram.com/nitaprose/?hl=en', '', 'https://www.nitaprose.com/', 1),
(20650398, 'Cara North', 'Cara North: contemporary, paranormal, and sci-fi romanceSeptember North: YA for mature readersEcho North: FantasyTonya Nagle, PhD: Non-fictionI\'ve been writing as Cara for over 15 years. In 2019, I merged everything under my Creative Writing With Dr Nagle website.', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1724982386p5/20650398.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/cara.northleoni/', 'https://www.instagram.com/caraodactyl/?hl=en', 'https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCt-pgyL7ddfIA9SSyYyA7QA', 'https://www.caranorth.net/', 1),
(20758478, 'Catherine Fogarty', 'No Description available', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/No-Image-Placeholder.svg/1665px-No-Image-Placeholder.svg.png', 'https://www.facebook.com/public/Catherine-Fogarty', 'https://www.instagram.com/cathfog/', 'https://www.youtube.com/@CatherineFogarty/featured', 'https://www.catherinebfogarty.com/', 1),
(20810392, 'Liz Scheier', '', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/No-Image-Placeholder.svg/1665px-No-Image-Placeholder.svg.png', 'https://www.facebook.com/BrynMawrCollege/photos/a.239117944891/10159190058154892/', 'https://www.instagram.com/lscheier/reels/?__d=11', '', 'https://www.lizscheier.com/', 1),
(20839299, 'Amanda Bestor-Siegal', 'AMANDA BESTOR-SIEGAL received her M.F.A. from the Michener Center for Writers, University of Texas, specializing in fiction and screenwriting. Amanda lived in France for four years before relocating to Austin, Texas, where she works at a kitten nursery.', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1628186560p5/20839299.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/BeverleyHasRead/', 'https://www.instagram.com/amandabestorsiegal/?hl=en', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=laY6G5JwJtg', 'https://www.amandabestorsiegal.com/', 1),
(20851054, 'Tabitha Lasley', 'Tabitha Lasley was a journalist for ten years. She has lived in London, Johannesburg, and Aberdeen. SEA STATE is her first book.', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1639526131p5/20851054.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/events/university-of-liverpool/masculinity-loneliness-and-female-desire-sea-state-with-tabitha-lasley/222572236584203/', 'https://www.instagram.com/tabithalasley/', 'https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCi-C3RdDfnLH9hRCcxjRbpQ/videos', 'https://granta.com/one-day-it-will-all-make-sense/', 1),
(20904455, 'Skye Alder', '', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1606208400p5/20904455.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/LaceSeries/photos/my-headspace-is-still-with-fable-and-alder-on-skye-and-i-aint-even-mad-their-sta/4861774917215203/', 'https://www.instagram.com/meganwadewrites/p/C8ejDmNhz5_/', 'https://www.youtube.com/@SkyeAlder-zw1zm/videos', 'https://books.apple.com/us/author/skye-alder/id1542438784', 1),
(20997389, 'Freya Sampson', 'Freya Sampson is the USA Today bestselling author of The Last Chance Library and The Lost Ticket/The Girl on the 88 Bus. She studied history at Cambridge University and worked in television as an executive producer, making documentaries about everything from the British royal family to neighbours from hell. She lives in London with her husband, children and cats. Nosy Neighbours is her third novel.', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1695396802p5/20997389.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/FreyaSampsonAuthor/', 'https://www.instagram.com/freyasampsonauthor/?hl=en', 'https://www.youtube.com/@freyasampson7043/shorts', 'https://freya-sampson.com/', 1),
(21087867, 'Maria   Anderson', '', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/No-Image-Placeholder.svg/1665px-No-Image-Placeholder.svg.png', 'https://www.facebook.com/public/Maria-Anderson/', 'https://www.instagram.com/maria_aanderson/?hl=en', 'https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC0_kaEUGSI0EpEm2qd5yF3w', 'https://mariananderson.exhibits.library.upenn.edu/', 1),
(21140919, 'Nikki Erlick', 'Nikki Erlick is a writer and editor whose work has appeared on the websites of New York magazine, Harper’s Bazaar, Newsweek, Cosmopolitan, The Huffington Post, Indagare Travel, BookTrib, and Verge Media. As a travel writer, she explored nearly a dozen countries on assignment—from rural villages in France to the arctic fjords of Norway. As a ghostwriter, she has lent her voice to CEOs, academics, and entrepreneurs. She graduated Harvard University summa cum laude and is a former editor of the Harvard Crimson. She earned a master’s degree in global thought from Columbia University. The Measure is her first novel.', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1646686994p5/21140919.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/photo.php?fbid=2847349908893958&id=1500073493621613&set=a.1540174859611476', 'https://www.instagram.com/nikkierlick/?hl=en', '', 'https://www.nikkierlick.com/', 1),
(21269624, 'Simone Gorrindo', '', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1689976079p5/21269624.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/simone.gorrindo/', 'https://www.instagram.com/simonegorrindo/?hl=en', '', 'https://www.simonegorrindo.com/', 1),
(21280926, 'Bessel van der Kolk', '​Bessel van der Kolk MD spends his career studying how children and adults adapt to traumatic experiences, and has translated emerging findings from neuroscience and attachment research to develop and study a range of treatments for traumatic stress in children and adults.In 1984, he set up one of the first clinical/research centers in the US dedicated to study and treatment of traumatic stress in civilian populations, which has trained numerous researchers and clinicians specializing in the study and treatment of traumatic stress, and which has been continually funded to research the impact of traumatic stress and effective treatment interventions. He did the first studies on the effects of SSRIs on PTSD; was a member of the first neuroima', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1617660077p5/21280926.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/thebodykeepsthescore/', 'https://www.instagram.com/bessel_van/?hl=en', 'https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC_mukO_G2AEAsgrBmdx6x_Q', 'https://www.besselvanderkolk.com/', 1),
(21302688, 'Azam Ahmed', '', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/No-Image-Placeholder.svg/1665px-No-Image-Placeholder.svg.png', 'https://www.facebook.com/p/Azam-Ahmed-official-100066778035955/?locale=is_IS', 'https://www.instagram.com/azamahmed/', 'https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC_PI-080Si-tyrdwaHA92eA', 'https://twitter.com/azamsahmed?lang=en', 1),
(21321678, 'Patricia Daniels Cornwell', 'see: Patricia Cornwell Patricia Cornwell\'s first title: \nPostmortem \nwas published under Patricia Daniels CornwellVarious editions of her other titles are published under Patricia D. Cornwell, which are also found here.', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/No-Image-Placeholder.svg/1665px-No-Image-Placeholder.svg.png', 'https://www.facebook.com/patricia.cornwell/', 'https://www.instagram.com/1pcornwell/?hl=en', 'https://www.youtube.com/@1pcornwell', 'https://www.facebook.com/patricia.cornwell/', 1),
(21370624, 'Bonnie Garmus', 'Bonnie Garmus is a copywriter and creative director who’s worked widely in the fields of technology, medicine, and education. She’s an open-water swimmer, a rower, and mother to two pretty amazing daughters. Born in California and most recently from Seattle, she currently lives in London with her husband and her dog, 99.', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1634023482p5/21370624.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/events/book-ish/an-evening-with-bonnie-garmus/1830239533840044/', 'https://www.instagram.com/bonnie_garmus_author/?hl=en', '', 'https://www.bonniegarmus.com/', 1),
(21373404, 'Coco Mellors', 'Coco Mellors is a writer from London and New York. She received her MFA in Fiction from New York University, where she was a Goldwater fellow. She currently lives in Los Angeles with her husband. Cleopatra and Frankenstein is her first novel.', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1623451446p5/21373404.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/WellRead.Page/videos/delighted-to-share-this-video-message-from-coco-mellors-author-of-this-months-se/474618194314059/', 'https://www.instagram.com/cocomellors/?hl=en', '', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coco_Mellors', 1),
(21416131, 'Emilia Hart', 'Emilia Hart is a British-Australian writer. She was born in Sydney and studied English Literature and Law at the University of New South Wales before working as a lawyer in Sydney and London.Emilia is a graduate of Curtis Brown Creative’s Three Month Online Novel Writing Course and was Highly Commended in the 2021 Caledonia Novel Award. Her short fiction has been published in Australia and the UK. \"Weyward\" is her debut novel. She lives in London, England.', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1678039694p5/21416131.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/emiliahartldn/', 'https://www.instagram.com/emiliahartbooks/?hl=en', 'https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCEB4aUI1vOsDnSZIDWSaWaA/videos', 'https://us.macmillan.com/author/emiliahart', 1),
(21427777, 'Jenny Pentland', 'No Description available', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/No-Image-Placeholder.svg/1665px-No-Image-Placeholder.svg.png', 'https://www.facebook.com/jenny.pentland/?locale=fy_NL', 'https://www.instagram.com/jennypentlandged/?hl=en', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SJi6EPLPKqs', 'https://www.facebook.com/jennypentlandGED/', 1),
(21445519, 'Noelle Crooks', 'A California native, Noelle Crooks’s love of books started at a young age when running to the local library with her late father. Before publishing her debut novel, Under the Influence, Noelle held roles at Sephora and Dolce Vita, and was the brand director at The Hollis Company. An education activist, Noelle is passionate about supporting youth literacy within marginalized schools. Noelle resides in New York City with her sidekick pup, Cooper.', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1691491615p5/21445519.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/noelle.crooks.1/', 'https://www.instagram.com/noellecrooks/?hl=en', 'https://www.youtube.com/user/noellebaby123', 'https://www.instagram.com/noellecrooks/?hl=en', 1),
(21567386, 'A.J. Moran', '', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1624620163p5/21567386.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/aj.moran930/', 'https://www.instagram.com/aj_moran_author/', 'https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCpzhzSrMJnsHMvO4NTcGUtA', 'https://www.ameripriseadvisors.com/alexandra.j.moran/', 1),
(21650052, 'Tara M. Stringfellow', 'Former attorney, Northwestern University MFA graduate, and Pushcart Prize nominee Tara M. Stringfellow’s debut novel Memphis (Dial Press, an imprint of Penguin Random House) is a multi-generational bildungsroman based on the author’s rich Civil Rights history.A recent winner of the Book Pipeline Fiction Contest, Memphis was recognized for its clear path to film or TV series adaptation and is due out in 2022. Third World Press published her first collection of poetry entitled More than Dancing in 2008.A cross-genre artist, the author was Northwestern University’s first MFA graduate in both poetry and prose and has been nominated for two Pushcart Prizes, as well as Best of the Net.Her poems have appeared in Collective Unrest, Jet Fuel Review,', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1649030955p5/21650052.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/tara.stringfellow.5/', 'https://www.instagram.com/tarastringfellow/?hl=en', '', 'https://www.tarastringfellow.com/', 1),
(21698259, 'Sophie Irwin', 'Sophie Irwin grew up in Dorset before moving to south London after university. She has spent years immersed in the study of historical fiction, from a dissertation on how Georgette Heyer helped win World War Two, to time spent in dusty stacks and old tomes losing herself in Regency London while researching this book. Her love and passion for historical fiction bring a breath of fresh air and a contemporary energy to the genre, and Sophie hopes to transport readers to a time when ballrooms were more like battlegrounds.', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/No-Image-Placeholder.svg/1665px-No-Image-Placeholder.svg.png', 'https://www.facebook.com/sophie.irwin.5/', 'https://www.instagram.com/sophieirwin__/', 'https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCgISf8HoD5mutPw1XPe6cTQ', 'https://www.instagram.com/sophie.irwin/?hl=en', 1),
(21711480, 'Brendan Slocumb', 'Brendan Nicholaus Slocumb was born in Yuba City, California and was raised in Fayetteville, North Carolina. He holds a degree in music education (with concentrations in violin and viola) from the University of North Carolina at Greensboro. For more than twenty years he has been a public and private school music educator and has performed with orchestras throughout Northern Virginia, Maryland, and Washington, DC. In his spare time, Brendan enjoys writing, exercising, collecting comic books and action figures, and performing with his rock band, Geppetto\'s Wüd.', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1681255485p5/21711480.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/AuthorBrendanSlocumb/', 'https://www.instagram.com/brendanslocumb/?hl=en', 'https://www.youtube.com/@SIBALAND', 'https://www.brendanslocumb.com/my-playlist', 1),
(21726154, 'Lindsey Fairleigh', '', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/No-Image-Placeholder.svg/1665px-No-Image-Placeholder.svg.png', 'https://www.facebook.com/groups/noshelfcontrolpodcast/', 'https://www.instagram.com/lindseyschwag/', 'https://www.youtube.com/c/AuthorLindseySparks', 'https://www.authorlindseysparks.com/', 1),
(21774719, 'Alison Fairbrother', '', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/No-Image-Placeholder.svg/1665px-No-Image-Placeholder.svg.png', 'https://www.facebook.com/alison.fairbrother.14/', 'https://www.instagram.com/adfairbro/', 'https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCs0ibJC2gKs27aifpd22G8g', 'https://www.alisonfairbrother.com/', 1),
(21941190, 'Belinda Huijuan Tang', 'I am a writer from San Jose, California.My debut novel, A Map for the Missing, is forthcoming from Penguin Press in August of 2022. Most recently, I was a Truman Capote Fellow at the Iowa Writers’ Workshop. Before that, I lived in Beijing and studied at Peking University for two years. In college I thought I would be an economist. My writing has received the Michener Copernicus Award and a Bread Loaf Work-Study Scholarship. Currently, I live in Los Angeles.', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1643258365p5/21941190.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/rachelbarenbaumauthor/', 'https://www.instagram.com/belinda.huijuan.tang/?hl=en', 'https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC-DqkL9jGflDC7mr3m6IafQ/videos', 'https://www.belindahuijuantang.com/', 1),
(22019548, 'LaToya Watkins', 'LaToya Watkins’s writing has appeared in A Public Space, The Sun, McSweeney’s, Kenyon Review, The Pushcart Prize Anthology (2015), and elsewhere. She has received grants, scholarships, and fellowships from the Bread Loaf Writers’ Conference, MacDowell Colony, Yaddo, Hedgebrook, and A Public Space (she was one of their 2018 Emerging Writers Fellows). She holds a PhD from the University of Texas at Dallas. Perish is her debut novel.', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/No-Image-Placeholder.svg/1665px-No-Image-Placeholder.svg.png', 'https://www.facebook.com/latoya.watkins.71/', 'https://www.instagram.com/drlwatkins/?hl=en', 'https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCwvp6oSN1UC4pgwX0vVJ8Dw', 'https://www.latoyawatkins.com/', 1),
(22049701, 'Olesya Salnikova Gilmore', 'Olesya Salnikova Gilmore is the author of The Witch and the Tsar. Originally from Moscow, she was raised in the US and graduated from Pepperdine University with a BA in English/political science, and from Northwestern School of Law with a JD. She practiced litigation at a large law firm for several years before pursuing her dream of becoming an author. Now she is happiest writing speculative historical fiction inspired by Eastern European history and folklore. Her work has appeared in LitHub, Tor.com, Historical Novels Review, Bookish, Washington Independent Review of Books, among others. She lives in a wooded, lakeside suburb of Chicago with her husband and daughter.', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1648050469p5/22049701.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/olesyaauthor/', 'https://www.instagram.com/olesyaauthor/', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=O2kvd3u_f4o', 'https://olesyagilmore.com/', 1),
(22208951, 'January Rayne', 'January Rayne is a pseudonym I decided to use because it sounds better than my given name. I’m a lover of all romance and write in the genres I love most because why limit myself? I want to write anything and everything, from badass men and women to characters who want to rip each other’s clothes off. I plan to ‘take it all’ like the good little girl I am.', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1645158958p5/22208951.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/AuthorJanuaryRayne/albums/178079441449093/', 'https://www.instagram.com/author_01rayne/', 'https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCFcKkyED3VFI-IkbRUuvbGQ', 'https://januaryrayneromance.com/', 1),
(22419488, 'Emma Rosenblum', 'Emma Rosenblum is the national bestselling author of Bad Summer People, Very Bad Company, and the upcoming Mean Moms (July, 2025). She\'s the former chief content officer at Bustle Digital Group, overseeing content and strategy for BDG’s editorial portfolios, including Bustle, Elite Daily, Romper, NYLON, The Zoe Report, Romper, Scary Mommy, Fatherly, The Dad, and Inverse. Prior to BDG, Emma served as the executive editor of ELLE. Previously Rosenblum was a senior editor at Bloomberg Businessweek, and before that a senior editor at Glamour. She began her career at New York magazine. She lives in New York City, with her husband and two sons.', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1670077524p5/22419488.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/emma.rosenblum.1/', 'https://www.instagram.com/emma.rosenblum/?hl=en', 'https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/emmarosenblum', 'https://www.emma-rosenblum.com/', 1),
(22458670, 'Ana  Reyes', 'Ana Reyes has an MFA from Louisiana State University. Her work has appeared in Bodega, Pear Noir!, The New Delta Review, and elsewhere. She lives in Los Angeles with her husband and teaches creative writing to older adults at Santa Monica College. The House in the Pines in her first novel.', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1654277284p5/22458670.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/anareyeswriter/', 'https://www.instagram.com/anareyeswriter/?hl=en', 'https://www.youtube.com/user/AMTV247/videos', 'https://www.anareyeswriter.com/', 1),
(22459580, 'Mikki Brammer', 'Mikki Brammer is from Tasmania, Australia and now lives in New York City by way of France and Spain. She writes about architecture, art and design for publications including Architectural Digest, ELLE Décor, and Dwell. The Collected Regrets of Clover is her first novel and has so far been published in 26 languages.', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1673636873p5/22459580.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/story.php/?story_fbid=952464640214760&id=100063536982038', 'https://www.instagram.com/mikkibrammer/?hl=en', 'https://www.youtube.com/@TheCentreofKi/videos', 'https://www.mikkibrammer.com/', 1),
(22476444, 'Jessa Maxwell', 'Jessa Maxwell lives In Jamestown, RI with her husband, cats and a three-legged dog. Follow her on Instagram @jessamaxwellauthor', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1666903286p5/22476444.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/jessa.maxwell.5/', 'https://www.instagram.com/jessamaxwellauthor/?hl=en', '', 'https://www.simonandschuster.com/authors/Jessa-Maxwell/193714745', 1),
(22487384, 'Kristen Perrin', 'Kristen Perrin is originally from Seattle, Washington, where she spent several years working as a bookseller before immigrating to the UK to do a Masters and PhD. She’s passionate about books and loves working on projects that have a mystery at their heart. She lives with her family in Surrey, where she can be found poking around vintage bookstores, stomping in the mud with her two kids, and collecting too many plants.Find her on Instagram: @kristenperrinwritesFind her on Tiktok: @kristen_perrin', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1693559920p5/22487384.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/KristinPerrinSommelierServices/', 'https://www.instagram.com/kristenperrinwrites/?hl=en', 'https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC0qdhBx14dkECIJbU4WTEpA', 'https://www.kristenperrin.com/', 1),
(22666715, 'Alan                Campbell', 'Alan wrote the Deepgate Codex and the Gravedigger Chronicles. He\'s still alive.', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1660084831p5/22666715.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/public/Alan-Campbell/', 'https://www.instagram.com/alancampbellnews/', 'https://www.youtube.com/user/TheWorryingWonton', 'https://www.alancampbell.net/', 1),
