(29566882, 'Amanda    Peters', 'Amanda Peters is a writer of Mi’kmaw and settler ancestry. Her work has appeared in the Antigonish Review, Grain Magazine, The Alaska Quarterly Review, the Dalhousie Review, and filling station magazine. She is the winner of the 2021 Indigenous Voices Award (IVA) for unpublished prose and a participant in the 2021 Writers Trust Rising Stars program. Amanda has a certificate in creative writing from the University of Toronto and she is a graduate of the Master of Fine Arts program at the Institute of American Indian Arts in Santa Fe New Mexico. Amanda is an Associate Professor in the Department of English and Theatre at Acadia University. She lives and writes in the Annapolis valley Nova Scotia with her fur babies Holly and Pook.', 'https://images.gr-assets.com/authors/1689690367p5/29566882.jpg', 'https://www.facebook.com/public/Amanda-Peters/', 'https://www.instagram.com/amandapetersauthor/?hl=en', 'https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCbuauNRCmoa6KD9W2xsFw-w', 'https://amandapetersauthor.com/', 1),
